  "query_preview": "(Today through Thursday)...\nIssued at 232 AM EDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nSurface analysis early this morning shows a cold front across \nsouthern Indiana near the Ohio River. Aloft, water vapor showed a \nridge axis stretching from the lower Mississippi to the northern \nplains states. GOES19 showed clear skies across much of Indiana and \npoints to the northwest, dominated by the high pressure system, \nwhile mainly high cloud was streaming across the plains states on \nthe windward side of the ridge axis. \n\nToday...\n\nThe upstream ridge will continue to produce subsidence \nacross the area as the surface high pressure system pushes southeast \ninto the Great Lakes, Indiana and Ohio. Forecast soundings remain \ndry through the day. Thus Mostly Sunny skies will be expected, along \nwith cooler high temperatures in the upper 60s to around 70.\n\nTonight and Saturday...\n\nThe ridge axis to the west is expected to push east of Indiana late \ntonight and Into Saturday. This will end subsidence across Indiana \nas windward side upglide begins. The first sign of this will be \ninvading CI this evening and into Saturday. Forecast soundings show \nsaturation aloft as the high clouds found to the west begin to reach \nIndiana. The lower levels remain very dry however. This will be due \nto the strong surface high pressure in place east of Indiana. Thus \ndry weather will be expected to tonight and Saturday as high clouds \nincrease across the area.\n\nSaturday Night and Sunday...\n\nA warm front is suggested to develop over Southern IL and western KY \nby Saturday night and begin to push across Indiana through Sunday \nmorning. The 300K GFS Isentropic surface shows moderate lift, with \nspecific humidities over 6 g/kg. Forecast soundings show a top down \nsaturation occurring through the overnight and into Sunday with \npwats around 1.3 inches. Meanwhile aloft, a moderate upper trough is \nsuggested to push in to Illinois and Indiana providing forcing. Thus \nthere are plenty of ingredients for rain during this time and \nconfidence is high for widespread measurable rain as these features \npass through Sunday. Clouds and precip will result in a cooler day \non Sunday with highs only in the lower 60s.\n\nMonday through Thursday...\n\nA wet and mild pattern is suggested to be in place for much of the \nnext work week. An upper trough is suggested to be over Indiana on \nMonday, with Sunday/s forcing dynamics exiting east. Still plenty of \nmoisture will remain in place as the 300K isentropic surface shows \nlift with high specific humidities near 6 g/kg. Forecast soundings \nstart the day with a saturated column, but dry air is shown to \nintrude into the column through the day. Thus pops will be needed \nmainly during the morning hours.\n\nModels suggest a much stronger upper trough over the plains on \nTuesday, poised to push toward Indiana by Thursday before becoming a \nclosed upper low over the Tennessee valley. Cyclonic flow will \nremain across the area through this period. Within the lower levels \nan associated strong surface low will be approaching from the \nplains, allowing for a warm and moist gulf flow streaming into the \nOhio valley. Forecast soundings through Thursday should periods of \ndeep saturation and high pwats as these upper dynamics remain \npassing through our region. Thus pops will need to be included on \nTuesday through Thursday. Temperatures will remain above normal \ngiven the warm and moist southerly flow, but cooler than we have \nseen this past week.",
